 "lines": [
  {
   "say": "The NES version of Metal Gear doesn't actually have a Metal Gear in it.",
   "scene": {
    "kind": "title",
    "prop": "sneak"
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "Metal Gear started on a Japanese computer called the M.S.X. two, in July 1987.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "desk",
    "head": "1987",
    "headsc": 4,
    "prop": "computer",
    "args": {
     "text": "MGEAR"
    },
    "subs": [
     "MSX2 COMPUTER"
    ]
   },
   "cap": "Metal Gear started on a Japanese computer called the MSX2, in July 1987."
  },
  {
   "say": "It was the first game Hideo Kojima ever directed.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "dark",
    "head": "HIDEO KOJIMA",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "award",
    "args": {
     "n": "1ST",
     "text": "GAME AS DIRECTOR"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "The computer couldn't handle lots of bullets and enemies on screen, so Kojima made a game about hiding instead of shooting.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "base",
    "head": "HIDE, DON'T SHOOT",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "sneak"
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "He was inspired by the movie, The Great Escape.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "dark",
    "head": "INSPIRATION",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "film",
    "args": {
     "t1": "THE GREAT ESCAPE",
     "t2": "1963"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "The NES version reached America in June 1988, published by Konami's second label, Ultra Games.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "space",
    "head": "1988",
    "headsc": 4,
    "prop": "port",
    "args": {
     "label": "METAL GEAR",
     "col": "grn"
    },
    "subs": [
     "ULTRA GAMES"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "But a different Konami team made it, and they changed a lot.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "dark",
    "head": "A NEW TEAM",
    "prop": "swap",
    "args": {
     "frm": "MSX2",
     "to": "NES",
     "frmcol": "blu",
     "tocol": "red",
     "at": 1.4
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "You now start by parachuting into a jungle.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "jungle",
    "head": "NEW OPENING",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "parachute"
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "And the final boss, the Metal Gear tank itself, was replaced by a supercomputer.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "base",
    "head": "SWAPPED",
    "headcol": "red",
    "prop": "nameswap",
    "args": {
     "frm": "METAL GEAR",
     "to": "A COMPUTER",
     "at": 1.8
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "The giant helicopter boss was swapped out too, for a pair of turret gunners.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "base",
    "head": "NO HELICOPTER",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "nameswap",
    "args": {
     "label": "BOSS FIGHT",
     "frm": "HELICOPTER",
     "to": "2 TURRETS",
     "at": 1.6
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "And instead of saving to tape, like the computer version, the NES game uses passwords.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "dark",
    "head": "PASSWORDS",
    "prop": "quote",
    "args": {
     "text": "PASSWORD: * * * * *",
     "col": "lblu"
    },
    "subs": [
     "NO TAPE SAVES"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "The translation was rough, too. One sleepy guard says: I feel asleep!",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "base",
    "head": "OOPS",
    "prop": "quote",
    "args": {
     "text": "I FEEL ASLEEP!!"
    },
    "subs": [
     "A SLEEPY GUARD"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "say": "Kojima later said the NES port wasn't up to his standards.",
   "scene": {
    "bg": "dark",
    "head": "KOJIMA'S VERDICT",
    "headsc": 2,
    "prop": "quote",
    "args": {
     "text": "WASN'T UP TO MY STANDARDS",
     "col": "red"
